    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). The only remaining references to the old field names are inside the acceptance test itself, which deliberately asserts those fields are gone.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single stored `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**New / renamed units (each with a single responsibility):**\n- **`model/MemberId.java`** (new) \u2014 single source of truth for the format: `format(region, fyShort, hash8)` builds the body and appends the Luhn `CHK` over its digits; `regionOf` / `fiscalYearShortOf` read the leading segments back (region = leading run of letters, FY = the two digits after it, so both survive a collision suffix).\n- **`service/MemberIdGenerator.java`** (renamed from `CustomerCodeGenerator`) \u2014 reuses the same `hash8` (SHA-256 over telephone+lastName, first 8 upper-hex) and now composes `MemberId.format`. `generateUnique` keeps the collision-suffix logic, now keyed on the member id.\n\n**Wiring changes:**\n- **`Owner`** \u2014 field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id`; `getPrimaryIdentifier()` returns the member id; `getMembershipNumber()` and `getCheckDigit()` removed; `getFiscalYear()` now derives its `FY<YY>` from the member id (falling back to the registration date before one is assigned); `getLocality()` parses the region from the member id (feeding `getOwnerSegment()`).\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 generates the member id with the fiscal year of the finalized (defaulted + business-day-rolled) registration date, deduped via `existsByMemberId`.\n- **`OwnerRepository`** + JDBC/JPA/Spring-Data impls \u2014 `existsByCustomerCode` \u2192 `existsByMemberId` (`member_id` column / `memberId` property).\n- **`OwnerAuditLogger`** + **`OwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 audit line and event now carry `memberId`.\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 ignore `memberId` on inbound mapping (server-assigned).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode` schema with `memberId`, removed `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` (the DTOs are generated from this at build time).\n- **DB schemas** (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres) \u2014 `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id`, widened to `VARCHAR(32)` to fit `UNKNOWN`-region ids plus any collision suffix.\n\nA sample audit line from the run confirms the shape: `memberId=NSW2616E6609E3` (region `NSW`, FY `26`, hash `16E6609E`, check `3`).",
